  "facts": [
    "Cadí Tunnel, a 5,026‑meter marvel, opened on 29 October 1984, linking the C-16 highway’s southern entrance at Gréixer, 1,175 m altitude, to its northern portal in Urús, 1,236 m high.",
    "Designed with two lanes separated by a 2‑meter safety zone, Cadí Tunnel’s engineering ensures safe passage beneath the Serra de Moixeró, a feat completed after a 1978 construction start under a 1973 license.",
    "Named after the nearby Serra del Cadí to avoid confusion with Serra de Moixeró, the tunnel sits within Cadí‑Moixeró Natural Park, sharing its landscape with the iconic Pedraforca peak."
